  description: 
  title: Hexadecimal Arithmetic and Bitwise Operations
  content: "Lesson 3: Hexadecimal Arithmetic and Bitwise Operations\r\nObjective:
    Learn to use hexadecimal values and perform bitwise operations.\n\r\nInstructions
    Covered:\r\nHexadecimal Values: Use 0x prefix to specify hex values, or just
    use the value if the context expects hex.\r\nAND, OR, XOR: Perform bitwise operations.\r\nMOV
    AL, 0xF0\r\nAND AL, 0x0F    ; AL becomes 0x00\r\nSHL (Shift Left): Shifts bits
    in a register to the left by a specified count.\r\nExercise Application: In Exercise
    5 (Logic Lizard) and Exercise 6 (Shifty Snake), you\u2019ll use AND to filter
    bits and SHL to multiply a value by powers of 2.\r\n\r\n"
